{"seq": 76, "missing": [{"zh": "锡晋斋因收藏晋代陆机手书《平复帖》而得名，但恭王府博物馆官方另一篇文章（媒体关注栏目）明确说明该帖现藏于故宫博物院；本条未说明《平复帖》现是否仍陈列于锡晋斋内，若游客专程为看这件'得名之由'的真迹而来，可能会落空。", "tier_sensitive": true, "en": "Xijinzhai was named for its collection of Lu Ji’s handwritten Pingfu Tie from the Jin dynasty, but another official article by the Prince Gong’s Mansion Museum (in the Media Attention section) explicitly states that the work is now housed at the Palace Museum; this entry does not state whether Pingfu Tie is still on display inside Xijinzhai, so visitors who come specifically to see the authentic work that gave the site its name may be disappointed."}], "found_factual_error": false, "error_note_zh": null, "top_missing_zh": "锡晋斋因收藏晋代陆机手书《平复帖》而得名，但恭王府博物馆官方另一篇文章（媒体关注栏目）明确说明该帖现藏于故宫博物院；本条未说明《平复帖》现是否仍陈列于锡晋斋内，若游客专程为看这件'得名之由'的真迹而来，可能会落空。", "top_missing_en": "Xijinzhai was named for its collection of Lu Ji’s handwritten Pingfu Tie from the Jin dynasty, but another official article by the Prince Gong’s Mansion Museum (in the Media Attention section) explicitly states that the work is now housed at the Palace Museum; this entry does not state whether Pingfu Tie is still on display inside Xijinzhai, so visitors who come specifically to see the authentic work that gave the site its name may be disappointed."}
